# No `version` or `date-released` on purpose: the version of record is
# .claude-plugin/plugin.json, a hand-typed copy here would be stale after the next
# release, and bin/heimdall-render-version renders only md, txt, json, toml, html, js,
# sh, yml and yaml files, so it would never reach a .cff file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "runhmd (hmd): a verification gate for AI coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: RJ
    alias: randomittin
repository-code: "https://github.com/randomittin/heimdall"
repository-artifact: "https://www.npmjs.com/package/runhmd"
url: "https://runheimdall.dev"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  hmd is a command-line test gate for AI coding agents that runs as git
  pre-commit and pre-push hooks. It makes an agent's work pass a test the
  agent did not write, and proves that test can fail, before the push lands.
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - verification
  - test gate
  - mutation testing
  - git hooks
  - quality gates
